## Automated Validation

For more efficient validation, the following tool sequence can be used:

```typescript
// 1. Identify changed files
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path '1000xbrain' -Recurse -Include '*.md' | Where-Object { $_.LastWriteTime -gt (Get-Date).AddHours(-24) }", false, false)

// 2. Check standard compliance
grep_search("@[^`]", false, "MODIFIED_FILES")
grep_search("^# |^## |^### ", false, "MODIFIED_FILES")

// 3. Read implementation plan
read_file("planning/feature-name/implementation.md", should_read_entire_file=true)

// 4. Check cross-references
grep_search("@knowledge/rules/[a-z0-9-]+\\.mdc", false, "MODIFIED_FILES")

// 5. Check content quality
grep_search("^## File Purpose and Relationship|^## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter|^## Command Format|^## Required Context|^## Process Steps|^## Expected Outputs|^## Error Handling", false, "MODIFIED_FILES")

// 6. Document validation results
edit_file("1000xbrain/workflows/rules-workflow/validation-results.md", 
          "Document change validation results",
          "# Change Validation Results\n\n...")
```

This validation process ensures that all implemented changes meet requirements, follow established standards, and integrate properly with the existing system. 